    "description": "A billing application is split into domain services, adapters and infrastructure code, but every service constructs its own collaborators: the invoice service news up a Postgres connection pool and a Stripe client in its constructor. Integration tests cannot replace them without patching module globals, the pool is created three times, and a staging incident happened because one service silently used the production DSN compiled into a helper. The team wants the application entry point to decide which concrete implementations exist, to hand each service what it needs, and to allow tests and the staging profile to supply fakes without touching service code. The decision to implement: how a service receives its collaborators from the outside instead of creating them, so configuration and tests control the concrete choices.",
    "decision_statement": "Have collaborators supplied from the outside at composition time so configuration and tests control concrete choices.",
    "notes": "Registry/separated-interface are the near-miss siblings a reviewer may prefer for a service locator style."
  },
